From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:12:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): a build of a session clone by its local path
 offers the clone's source

The card of a Code from External action that builds or runs a repo cloned earlier in the session offered no source when the command named the clone by a bare relative name (cmake -S melonDS, make -C melonDS, pip install -e melonDS), because only path-like words (with a slash or a leading dot) were matched against the session's fetched paths. A bare name under the run directory now counts too, except for the programs that only fetch or print it.

A clone made with a harmless git config (-c advice.detachedHead=false) lost its origin because every -c option marked the clone as one that runs code. Only config keys that can name a program do now.
---
